+# Application / database compatibility and staging release gates
+
+The active database observations below are supplied by the user's final directive on 2026-11-09. They were not independently queried in this task. No deployed application build identifier was supplied: “application” below means the current workspace source, not a verified deployed binary. The read-only [preflight](preflight.sql) provides executable checks for an authorized operator.
+
+## Compatibility matrix
+
+| Application feature | Required capability / source evidence | Supplied active DB evidence | Decision before release |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Queued auction comment processing | `lib/features/commerce/auction-server.ts:697` calls `process_live_auction_comment`; final source requires numeric author guard, source-time confirmation floor, winner-only finalization | Active public RPC is legacy: null-only author check, immediate order on host close, no confirmation floor | **BLOCKED.** Installing frontend/poller changes does not replace this SQL. Apply the complete required suffix after prerequisites pass. |
+| Manual close | `app/api/live-cf/auction/close/route.ts:15` calls `finalize_live_auction` | Public comment flow is reported to use a legacy immediate-order finalizer | **BLOCKED** until audit 1 installs confirmation-only close and audit 2/source fingerprint checks pass. Do not validate only `finalize_live_auction_highest_bid`: the public routing/finalizer path matters. |
+| Browser timer GET / expiry POST | `app/api/live-cf/auction/timer/route.ts:9`–15 calls `close_due_live_auction` and selects `ends_at`, `duration_seconds` | Required timer RPC and all three timer columns absent | **BLOCKED.** Deadlines migration provides schema/RPCs; audit 1 is also required for safe no-order expiry. |
+| Explicit start of a legacy round's timer | Timer route `:47` calls `start_legacy_auction_timer(uuid,uuid)` | Availability not supplied; timer schema absent | **BLOCKED** until deadlines and safe finalizers are installed. Existing rounds keep NULL deadlines unless explicitly started; no invented historical deadline. |
+| Workspace save with duration | `save_auction_workspace(uuid,uuid,uuid,jsonb)` deadline wrapper persists `durationSeconds`; `supabase/live-auction-deadlines.sql:124` | Current save RPC signature/body not supplied | **UNVERIFIED / BLOCKED** until preflight and staging save/replay checks pass. Legacy saves may ignore duration despite accepting JSON. |
+| Authenticated worker cron | Current `app/api/cron/facebook-webhooks/route.ts:26` calls **`expire_live_auctions_report`**, exposing `auctionExpiry` | `expire_live_auctions` absent; report RPC not confirmed | **BLOCKED.** Report RPC is installed by audit 2. An RPC failure is surfaced as `failed:1,unavailable:true`; HTTP 200 from the cron is not proof expiry worked. |
+| Existing integer expiry caller / optional SQL cron | `expire_live_auctions(uuid)` remains integer-compatible; audit 2 delegates to the reporting RPC | Integer RPC absent | **BLOCKED** until full suffix is installed. Failed counts are returned through report RPC; legacy callers retain integer result and queryable error ledger. |
+| Poll cursor reads / continuation writes | Poll route `:174`, `:300` uses `auction_poll_cursors`, including continuation-anchor/boundary metadata; audit 1 defines these and browser revocations | Table/columns/grants not included in supplied audit | **UNVERIFIED / BLOCKED** until catalogue/grant checks pass. Audit 1 not previously run does not by itself prove every individual object is absent. |
+| Graph query parameters / pagination validation | Poll route requests reverse chronological stream with `live_filter=no_filter`, exact HTTPS Graph version/video/comments paths, sanitized saved URLs | Not a SQL capability; real Meta diagnostic evidence still absent | Local request-validation tests pass. No claim that these parameters repair missing identities; live validation remains external. Whole auction flow is still blocked by legacy SQL. |
+| Workspace hydration and degraded form | Workspace GET returns 404 for missing explicit session, 503/degraded on failed reads; form blocks mutations while degraded | Live session/auction query health and delivery-review grants not supplied | **UNVERIFIED.** `ready:true` means hydration succeeded, not that installed SQL has safe winner semantics. This endpoint is not a migration readiness certificate. |
+| Delivery-review list | Workspace tenant-scoped `auction_deliveries` join returns channel/status only; dashboard `LiveSessionDashboard.tsx:488` renders review alert/list | Delivery table schema/grants not supplied | Verify preflight plus owner-session staging API/UI checks. No browser grants to protected tables should be added to bypass server failures. |
+| Expiry audit diagnostics | Audit 2 creates RLS-protected `auction_expiry_failures(sqlstate,auction_id,occurred_at)` and service-only report RPC | Not confirmed in active audit | **BLOCKED** until audit 2. Do not infer success from an empty error log when the reporting infrastructure is absent. |
+
+All source line references are for this workspace revision; use the logical patch/report to identify the reviewed code. Confirm the actual deployed commit/build before comparing runtime behavior.
+
+## Known migration suffix and preflight interpretation
+
+1. Run `preflight.sql` as an authorized operator. It is a `READ ONLY` transaction using catalogue metadata only; it does not call application RPCs or inspect customer/order/message rows. Missing objects return `BLOCKED`, including on an empty database.
+2. Every `00_base` row must pass **before** deadlines. If any is blocked, resolve missing prerequisite migrations from the complete registry first; the supplied audit does not establish which entire prefix is installed. Do not infer a migration was applied merely because a similarly named function exists.
+3. Required known suffix: **`live-auction-deadlines.sql` → `live-auction-audit-hardening.sql` → `live-auction-audit-hardening-2.sql`**. Registry order: `scripts/build-full-database-setup.cjs:145`–147; explicit dependencies: `:321`–323. Audit 1 has never run in the supplied active audit and must not be skipped. Audit 2 alone does not create timer columns or replace the legacy public finalizer.
+4. After deadlines, `10_before_audit_1` must pass. After audit 1, `20_before_audit_2` must pass. Release only after all `30_application` rows and the behavior rehearsal pass. Later-stage BLOCKED results are expected on the reported baseline and must not be treated as permission to skip earlier gates.
+5. Financial body checks compare MD5 of CRLF-normalized `pg_proc.prosrc` against reviewed source compiled in local PGlite; no function body is printed by the preflight. The reproducible staging test compares actual `pg_get_functiondef` before/after and final-vs-fresh definitions. Any body difference, including extra formatting, blocks release pending review. Digests are drift checks, not credentials or proof of behavior. Presence checks alone cannot prove all transitive financial dependencies or data invariants.
+6. Preflight does not read migration ledger rows, assert job/scheduler execution, verify package entitlement, or establish a live UI/Meta session. Review the ledger and checksums privately after its table/columns pass. Follow the unchanged checksum guard; do not replace recorded checksums to force migration replay.
+
+## Staging rehearsal and rollout order
+
+1. Build a disposable staging environment from an approved baseline/registry prefix. For a production-like clone, an authorized operator must establish its provenance and protect/redact customer data; this agent's PGlite simulation is not such a clone. Replay the **whole required registry prefix and suffix**, not audit 2 alone. Keep credentials and real Meta transport out of automated fixtures.
+2. Capture preflight output and installed public function definitions privately. Confirm the supplied legacy properties and missing timer capabilities. Seed synthetic numeric bidder IDs and a host in isolated staging. Demonstrate legacy immediate order creation before the upgrade; preserve that legacy order for a non-destructive comparison.
+3. Quiesce auction writes and worker execution for the staged upgrade. Preserve durable webhook ingress/queueing if supported; do not process queued bids against intermediate financial definitions. Inventory and suspend relevant external/database schedulers through the approved operator process. **The deadlines migration can schedule a pg_cron job if that extension exists** (`live-auction-deadlines.sql:164`–165); account for this side effect before applying it. PGlite has no pg_cron extension and does not exercise hosted job scheduling.
+4. Apply missing migrations in registry order with the established ledger/checksum mechanism. The automated rehearsal uses progressively generated **in-memory** complete-schema transactions; stored bundles are untouched. Standalone SQL files contain their own BEGIN/COMMIT: wrapping concatenated files in another transaction is not a substitute for a migration runner's verified atomicity. Do not expose an intermediate deadlines-only installation to writers/workers.
+5. Verify old rounds retain NULL deadlines and existing legacy orders are neither deleted nor re-invoiced. Inventory previously created orders separately; no retrospective financial repair is authorized here. Confirm new rounds receive deadlines, explicit timer start is idempotent, not-due is a no-op, pending queue yields draining, and due/no-queue locks a winner without an order.
+6. Run the real parser flow: two bidders → trusted host close → no order → genuinely pre-round/older confirmation stale → same-second winner confirmation → one order → replay → still one order. Audit 1 alone should demonstrate the source-seconds race; audit 2 must resolve it. Capture definitions at each stage, compare final definition with a fresh current-source installation, and investigate every unexplained difference.
+7. Run privacy/pagination/workspace/financial tests, test the expiry failure ledger/counts, and verify tenant/RLS/grant boundaries. Check application compatibility gates before releasing the app. Run an authenticated cron in staging and inspect `auctionExpiry.failed`/`unavailable`, then confirm the real external scheduler separately. Resume workers/writes only after successful verification.
+8. Production execution remains an operator-only follow-up. This task prepares artifacts and local evidence; it neither applies the sequence nor verifies current production state. Keep the identity-unverified phase gate until sanitized real Meta diagnostics arrive.
+
